WEBVTT

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:17.170
I was curious about who was interested 
enough in my best friend to come visit him...

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:21.230
But I'm not ready to join Gaston 
on the other side just yet.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.000
<b>Who Has the Black Notebook?</b>

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.080
Sorry for spooking you like that.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.250
It's fine, really.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.890
To Gaston's soul...

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.040
May he rest in peace.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.020
I found the rat you were 
looking for, Guillaume.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.030
He's actually with an old acquaintance.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.910
What? Why would he be hanging around Lupin?

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.100
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.420
Procure the package. Then, take him out.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.790
Which one?

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.380
Both of them!

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.450
So did you know Gaston long?

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:48.000
No, we met in this inn, and wound up 
becoming drinking buddies.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.810
How about you? How do you know Gaston?

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.090
Me?

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:58.310
You could say he taught me 
a thing or two when I was a nipper.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.840
Well, "ultimately, life is little 
more than a series of partings."

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:06.020
"If nothing else, raise a glass in their honor."

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.950
That's what it says in the Bible.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.450
Come now. That's not any piece 
of scripture I've ever heard of.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.530
I'm not lying! I'm a man of faith, y'know.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.710
See? That was the very page it was from.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.930
No. It wasn't.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:35.600
Nothing of the sort was 
written on that page.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.480
Oh, really?

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.520
That's pretty impressive, though.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:45.620
Knowing exactly what was on that page
when you only caught a glimpse of it.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.640
Being able to memorize something at a glance, 
as though you've taken a picture of it...

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.120
I guess that's what they call a 
"photographic memory," huh?

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.290
The hotshot investigator who 
could memorize everything,

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.290
from the state of a crime scene
 to the face of a suspect,

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.880
keeping everything on file in his mind
 so he could solve the case.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.380
Camille Bardot.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.510
You're kind of a celebrity among us thieves.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.360
To think that someone who made 
a living remembering faces

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.010
actually has a face that's
recognizable to a thief...

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.520
What a ridiculous state of affairs.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.880
Well, you don't look like you used to,

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.100
so I wasn't 100% positive.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.820
But my curiosity about
 this thing is killing me,

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.780
so I dangled some bait to see who'd bite.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.760
And I fell for it hook, line, and sinker.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.910
I suppose I chose the right 
time to retire, Lupin.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:37.660
So my face is in your files, 
huh? That's an honor.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.790
Hello. Who is this?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.800
<i>It's been a while, Louise.</i>

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.020
<i>It's me. You know who.</i>

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.050
Gaston?!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.810
<i>I would like you to deliver a message for me.</i>

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:55.940
<i>If a man in a blue jacket with a face that 
would look better on a monkey shows up—</i>

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.180
Why don't you just cut the crap?

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:02.260
<i>Oh, Lupin. Seems you completed 
the job I asked you to do for me.</i>

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:06.830
<i>I'm really looking forward 
to you delivering it to me.</i>

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:10.050
<i>Surely you're not thinking of refusing?</i>

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.450
<i>After all, you were paid in advance.</i>

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:17.870
Albert, it's you, isn't it?

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.840
<i>If that's what you believe, 
come and see for yourself.</i>

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.720
<i>I'll be waiting, Lupin.</i>

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:24.860
Dammit.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.430
Enter.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.640
Jose and his men are making their move.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.610
Most likely, under the orders 
of Director Guillaume.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.500
Turning to a washed-up spy who 
reinvented himself as an assassin...

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.350
He must be desperate.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.990
Jose's men are good at their jobs.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:46.860
If Lupin falls into their hands...

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.660
I wouldn't worry.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.780
Lupin has a knack for making himself scarce.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:54.770
Go.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.280
Get down!

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:10.920
What in the world was that?!

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.860
My car's out back. We can use it to get away!

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.470
A device that works as 
a universal smart key?

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.230
Must be convenient.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.390
A tool of the trade.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:48.130
When did the DGSE get so damn crazy?

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.820
It probably started out that way, actually.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:53.230
The only person who'd do something 
this outrageous is Jose.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.360
He used to be an undercover agent.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.560
But after spending too 
much time in deep cover,

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.320
he ended up picking up a lot of bad habits.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.460
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.590
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.710
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.590
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.340
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.090
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:31.590
<b>Lupin</b>

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:48.760
Doesn't he realize the whole reason I gave 
him a phone was for times like this?

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.750
And now, he doesn't even pick up.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.950
The guy's a walking anachronism, after all.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:27.530
You okay back there, Gramps?

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.350
I-I'm fine...

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:33.810
Sure doesn't sound like it.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:35.140
Jump out at the same time.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.000
One, two, three!

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:42.820
What?!

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:34.800
Gramps!

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.510
Sorry I dragged you into this.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:20.120
No... I'm the one who got you involved.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:26.390
What exactly do you know about 
the black notebook, Lupin?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.720
Not a whole lot.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:34.390
Though, if I were to guess, 
before the original was destroyed,

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:40.650
you memorized its contents, and got 
Gaston to make a perfect replica of it.

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:45.050
So you've figured it all out...

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.870
Seems like a lot of work 
went into it, but...

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.430
Why would you bother to make 
a facsimile of the black notebook?

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:56.270
I was a law enforcement 
professional for many years.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:11:01.480
I know full well that, sometimes, 
you have to turn a blind eye

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.390
in order to keep the house of cards upright.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:09.030
But the things in that black notebook...

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:12.300
It was my hope that, someday, 
when circumstances allowed,

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:16.650
everything in it would be made public.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.710
Someday, huh?

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:22.650
I have a hard time believing 
it'll ever happen.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:30.530
But before that day could come,
 someone realized we'd made a copy...

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.300
Guillaume from the Directorate-General 
for External Security, right?

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.110
Yes.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:40.550
He started making demands, telling us to
hand the replica notebook over to him.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.890
Considering it's as good as the real thing,

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:47.550
he'd have a lot of bigwigs over a barrel 
with its potential for blackmail.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:53.340
Guillaume will stop at nothing
to get what he wants.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:59.760
Hiding it in the usual way would have just
made him torture people until he had it...

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:04.980
So we hid it someplace he'd 
have no way of getting to it...

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.090
and then, told him as much.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:12.200
After that, he stopped hounding you guys?

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:17.700
Lupin... What are you going 
to do with that notebook?

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.350
Nothing whatsoever.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.760
But if I <i>have</i> to choose a course of action,

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:27.220
I might end up using it to slap Albert 
around a bit for saddling me with it.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.440
I see...

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.370
So what do we do now?

00:12:58.200 --> 00:12:59.600
We go see him.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.920
The last guy I ever wanted to see again...

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.550
This bugs me.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:40.580
What does?

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:45.790
We left Paris like it was no big deal, 
but now, we have to sneak back in.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:48.170
It's like we're being guided somewhere.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:51.170
Then, I say we graciously 
accept the invitation.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:55.630
Lupin, it's a trap. You oughta know that.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:14:00.700
And you ought to know that I'll use it as 
an opportunity to get the drop on him.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:05.200
Usually, I wouldn't try to stop you...

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.850
But you don't seem your usual self.

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:12.190
You're hot under the collar, like you 
used to get when you were younger.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.140
Does this Albert guy really—

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:27.210
No way. Are you serious?

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:28.550
Of course I am.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:32.490
I mean, he's a real hunk. 
And a director at his age to boot...

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.040
He might even become the 
minster of the interior someday.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.590
I've got bad news for you. 
Albert's already taken.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:40.000
What? Really?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.200
Some photographer who goes 
by the name of Tickey.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:45.200
They've been together for a 
while now, from what I hear.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.030
Oh, well...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:50.570
And here I was, thinking I had 
a chance at the jackpot.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.940
Tickey Pasco... That must be the guy.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:02.640
Guess his taste in men hasn't changed.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:09.470
If you don't wanna see him, 
why bother going?

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.280
It was so much fun!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.080
Yeah.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.120
Let's go again sometime!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.380
<b>You have one 
new message</b>

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.090
<b>You have one
 new message</b>

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:55.900
Here.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.890
M-Merci.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.740
Good choice.

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.910
Are we celebrating something today?

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.930
More of a pre-celebration.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:41.950
Albert...

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.430
I found this on the back of your suit.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.010
The Saint Martin Hotel at eight o'clock...

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.240
Guess I'll have to take a rain check 
on the meal you made.

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:55.710
Are you going to be late?

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:57.630
No, it shouldn't take long.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:59.550
Keep the soup warm for me.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.500
Are you Mr. Albert d’Andrésy?

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:31.060
Yes, that's me.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.580
I have a message for you. Here you are.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.320
Newfoundland Bridge

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:41.110
Ever the romantic, aren't you, Lupin?

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.780
I've been waiting for you, Lupin.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.030
I trust you've brought me what I asked you to?

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.310
Yeah, just like you wanted.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:27.050
This whole stupid setup, though... 
Why drag me into this?

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.530
Didn't have the guts to steal it yourself?

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.290
Hardly.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:37.790
But dirty jobs are best handled by 
dirty individuals, wouldn't you say?

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:42.770
You haven't changed one bit.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.230
That attitude is what always 
screws things up for you.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:50.320
You think I'll hand this over 
after what you just said?

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:54.300
I can always take it by force.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:59.180
So theft is too "dirty" for you, but 
shooting someone in cold blood is fine?

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.830
Yeah, your hands must be <i>real </i>clean.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:04.820
Why would shooting a sneak thief 
mean dirtying my hands?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.040
What's wrong?

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.300
Surprised that the gun you thought 
you'd swapped out is firing live bullets?

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:36.270
You wanted to get the drop on me 
as payback for roping you into this...

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.770
And it's that attitude of yours 
that screws things up for you.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:45.910
I didn't aim for your heart 
for a reason. Wanna know why?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.790
Because I wanted you to witness 
my moment of victory.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:41.140
Sorry, but I tossed the little toy you 
rigged my car with into the river.

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:18.850
I am Goemon Ishikawa.

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:21.810
Deceit begets deception, as the black 
notebook changes hands again and again.

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:26.240
With our knowledge of its contents, 
treacherous hands grasp for our necks.

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:29.470
I see. It seems our enemy 
is also not without skill.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:33.400
Lupin, leave our assailants to my blade.

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:37.710
You must concentrate your efforts 
on settling your old vendetta.

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:40.530
Next Time: The Man Who Abandoned "Lupin."

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>The Man Who Abandoned "Lupin".</b>

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:42.150
Unpleasant ties are hard to break.

00:22:42.150 --> 00:22:44.280
And the bonds between men 
cannot be severed by a sword.
